# mkfs.pdxfs — caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md). Adopted at
# R90-XREPO.013.M4-001 (paideia-os#2131 §2.1, this repo's issue #23),
# replacing the R53-vintage prose declaration this file used to carry
# (see git history for the superseded freeform "consumed_kinds" text
# and its per-milestone wiring notes).
#
# `!KIND_FOO <mask>` = mandatory: exec fails -EACCES if the parent's
# cap-set does not hold at least this mask. ` KIND_FOO <mask>` (no
# `!`) = optional: narrowed to at most this mask, dropped to zero if
# the parent held none. See the format doc §3.1 / §4 for the full
# narrowing semantics.

!KIND_USER               0x001   # invoker attribution (audit)
!KIND_PDXFS_FILE         0x003   # READ + WRITE (file-backed target)
 KIND_BLKDEV             0x00F   # open+write+flush+query (device target)
 KIND_SIG_KEY            0x001   # superblock re-sign, placeholder seed
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       0x001   # semantic-pipe stdout, deferred

# Notes (carried forward from the R53 prose decl + the M4-001 adoption
# inventory, design/user/fs-tools-caps.md §2.1):
#
# - KIND_USER and KIND_PDXFS_FILE are mandatory: mkfs cannot produce a
#   valid superblock without invoker attribution and without a target
#   to write.
# - KIND_BLKDEV is optional because a file-target run never touches
#   it; device-target runs (mkfs.pdxfs.M3-005, device-cap URI parsing)
#   are the only path that needs it. KIND_BLKDEV = 0x42
#   (src/kernel/core/cap/kind_blkdev.pdx) is the landed kind — the
#   design-doc name `KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE` used across this repo's own
#   comments (src/target.pdx, src/elevate_wire.pdx) is a doc-alias for
#   the same kind, not a distinct one (naming gap resolved per
#   design/hardware/nvme-ahci-tail-milestones.md §3.1; see
#   src/target.pdx's module header for the full history).
# - KIND_SIG_KEY is optional and unbound at this landing: no code path
#   mints or holds one yet (src/format.pdx signs with a placeholder
#   all-zero seed, a raw pointer, not a cap slot). Reserved so the
#   eventual real bind is a rights-narrow, not a decl amendment.
# - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT is optional and unbound: stdout is still a plain
#   sys_write of a human-readable line (src/format_record.pdx); the
#   semantic-pipe framing lands at mkfs.pdxfs.M3-003.
# - KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL is deliberately ABSENT from this decl: mkfs
#   elevates on demand per the R90-XREPO.011 elevate-broker policy and
#   never holds an elevate cap ambiently at exec time (matches the
#   `rm` pattern the round plan pins). src/elevate_wire.pdx's
#   mkfs_elev_require_device_write remains a fail-closed stub for this
#   same reason — it holds no KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL to call through.
#
# See also:
#   design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md  — format spec (paideia-os)
#   design/user/fs-tools-caps.md §2.1        — this tool's target cap-set
#   src/kernel/core/cap/reconcile.pdx        — kernel substrate
